1
00:01:36,390 --> 00:02:03,970
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:08,480
No living creature was hurt during the
production of this show.

3
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,320
Erlik Khan!

4
00:04:11,143 --> 00:04:12,553
You made me...

5
00:04:13,502 --> 00:04:17,312
talk to your soul.

6
00:04:26,187 --> 00:04:36,977
- Talks in Mongol -

7
00:04:38,813 --> 00:04:45,583
- Talks in Mongol -

8
00:05:15,576 --> 00:05:17,636
What have souls told you...

9
00:05:19,145 --> 00:05:21,605
about Noyan?

10
00:05:32,139 --> 00:05:35,499
You shall not mention...

11
00:05:36,452 --> 00:05:38,152
the holy name of my father!

12
00:05:48,272 --> 00:05:54,152
Everybody in Sogut is talking about your
victory, Togay.

13
00:05:54,613 --> 00:05:57,543
Only an idiot prides on his victory.

14
00:06:01,324 --> 00:06:06,454
The greater the victory is,
the greater the pain is.

15
00:06:09,037 --> 00:06:11,447
What do you want, Petrus?

16
00:06:11,601 --> 00:06:17,071
To distroy Osman's dignity which
has taken damage.

17
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:20,900
It has been done.

18
00:06:22,508 --> 00:06:24,858
Now it's time to shed blood.

19
00:06:26,696 --> 00:06:29,286
I thought you wanted brother blood.

20
00:06:30,185 --> 00:06:35,465
My father Noyan told me to get faster
to drink Osman's blood.

21
00:06:36,681 --> 00:06:38,061
Why?

22
00:06:40,289 --> 00:06:44,459
My father told me Osman
is a Gokboru.

23
00:06:53,045 --> 00:06:54,985
Wolves...

24
00:06:55,961 --> 00:06:58,621
went through Khan Tengri Mountain.

25
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:02,950
There are four classes of wolves.

26
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:10,076
Grey-maned wolf destroys all the herd when
he attacks.

27
00:07:10,076 --> 00:07:13,295
But eats only one of them.

28
00:07:13,295 --> 00:07:15,985
They are relentless.

29
00:07:16,481 --> 00:07:23,531
Maned wolves destroys half of the
herd when he attacks.

30
00:07:24,133 --> 00:07:27,553
Eats only one of them.

31
00:07:27,767 --> 00:07:30,147
They have a moral code sometimes.

32
00:07:33,227 --> 00:07:34,707
Bozkurt...

33
00:07:37,726 --> 00:07:43,428
destroys only one in a herd...

34
00:07:43,428 --> 00:07:46,633
eats half of it...

35
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:51,973
takes the other half to his herd.

36
00:07:53,624 --> 00:07:57,564
Bozkurts have manners.

37
00:08:01,139 --> 00:08:03,379
What about Gokboru?

38
00:08:06,826 --> 00:08:11,876
Gokboru... Gokboru...

39
00:08:11,946 --> 00:08:15,596
The wolf with sky-like feathers

40
00:08:16,227 --> 00:08:22,516
The wolf that Oguz Khan mentioned,
that lives once in a thousand years.

41
00:08:22,516 --> 00:08:31,596
When that wolf joins the herd, he makes
the herd stronger, thougher.

42
00:08:37,238 --> 00:08:40,718
The shamans which connects me
to my father...

43
00:08:43,253 --> 00:08:47,873
told me that Osman is a Gokboru.

44
00:08:54,623 --> 00:09:02,123
Osman will attack my herd only for me.

45
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:07,470
Only for me.

46
00:09:11,735 --> 00:09:16,865
That's why I have to move first.

47
00:09:22,250 --> 00:09:28,350
I am here to offer you something
that can make your herd stronger.

48
00:09:32,876 --> 00:09:38,456
- Who?
- Inegol's Lord Nicola.

49
00:09:55,024 --> 00:10:00,126
My Bala! We should do our best.
We should make her better.

50
00:10:03,446 --> 00:10:05,606
Inshallah, my Bey.

51
00:10:06,067 --> 00:10:08,417
You can mind your own business.

52
00:10:17,938 --> 00:10:21,068
She is here because she accepted
our invitation.

53
00:10:22,590 --> 00:10:24,600
She is entrusted to us.

54
00:10:27,643 --> 00:10:30,443
I surely will be taking good care of her.

55
00:10:53,992 --> 00:10:56,932
It's not so deep, thank Allah.

56
00:10:59,123 --> 00:11:02,473
I have no time to lose for
a little wound.

57
00:11:10,601 --> 00:11:15,671
He wounded my father, killed
my Alps.

58
00:11:16,841 --> 00:11:19,661
I'll find Togay and kill him!

59
00:11:22,414 --> 00:11:25,824
You may not be as lucky as
this next time.

60
00:11:37,495 --> 00:11:40,135
Sorry to hear what happened.

61
00:11:46,089 --> 00:11:48,999
I'm sorry to hear what happened,
Malhun Hatun.

62
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:55,150
I heard you were wounded...

63
00:11:55,716 --> 00:11:58,426
you have been brought to the tent...

64
00:11:59,894 --> 00:12:02,364
in the arms of Osman Bey.

65
00:12:13,809 --> 00:12:19,249
Apparently, our Osman Bey values you
very much.

66
00:12:23,502 --> 00:12:29,992
What was he supposed to do, Hazal Hatun?
Should his Alps have carried me? Come on.

67
00:12:34,564 --> 00:12:37,774
He respects my father Umur Bey.

68
00:12:41,642 --> 00:12:47,402
Of course, of course he does.

69
00:12:48,210 --> 00:12:51,480
He carried you himself because
he respects your father Umur Bey.

70
00:13:13,692 --> 00:13:17,902
My Bey, Savcı Bey and Lena Hatun took off
with their Alps.

71
00:13:18,073 --> 00:13:19,743
What about the guest Beys?

72
00:13:20,121 --> 00:13:23,631
They are returning to their tents under
our Alps' security.

73
00:13:26,182 --> 00:13:30,092
What di that infidel do, Osman Bey?

74
00:13:30,188 --> 00:13:33,898
Togay, Bamsı Bey, Togay.

75
00:13:34,669 --> 00:13:37,439
He attacked Malhun Hatun's alps.

76
00:13:38,937 --> 00:13:43,862
This Togay will cause so much trouble
if we don't make a move.

77
00:13:43,862 --> 00:13:48,072
Let him be, Uncle.

78
00:13:48,902 --> 00:13:54,022
We are going to bother him, no worries.

79
00:13:55,341 --> 00:14:00,161
As long as we are together, he can't
do anything, my Bey.

80
00:14:00,166 --> 00:14:03,677
We bait him with his own bait!

81
00:14:03,677 --> 00:14:09,539
We should also find the betrayer
in us and punish him...

82
00:14:09,539 --> 00:14:13,639
while considering Togay on the other hand.

83
00:14:18,239 --> 00:14:21,019
Nicola will return eventually.

84
00:14:21,638 --> 00:14:25,228
Jackals and pigs will make an alliance.

85
00:14:25,659 --> 00:14:31,621
If we unite, neither jackals nor pigs
can stop us.

86
00:14:33,401 --> 00:14:38,111
This was why Togay attacked the meeting
and tried to kill Beys.

87
00:14:38,517 --> 00:14:43,247
However, we are dealing with so much
things including Togay.

88
00:14:46,752 --> 00:14:54,232
Davut Bey is right. When Nicola returns,
they are going to make an alliance.

89
00:14:57,049 --> 00:14:59,759
But Bamsı Bey is also right.

90
00:15:02,383 --> 00:15:09,233
Jackals and pigs cannot stop us.

91
00:15:10,388 --> 00:15:15,458
Listen to me carefully now. I am
announcing my new goal.

92
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:42,763
What are you doing?

93
00:15:42,763 --> 00:15:44,903
That's what jackals do.

94
00:16:08,015 --> 00:16:10,305
They are nine.

95
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:17,190
They walked side by side till here,
They went on in single file.

96
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:37,380
They must be near.

97
00:16:38,079 --> 00:16:39,859
Let's go.

98
00:17:04,490 --> 00:17:06,410
Hide.

99
00:17:58,543 --> 00:18:00,393
Ambush!

100
00:18:08,149 --> 00:18:09,969
Attack!

101
00:19:25,816 --> 00:19:27,692
Suci.

102
00:19:27,692 --> 00:19:31,052
Cerkutay, my brother!

103
00:19:31,306 --> 00:19:35,296
Don't worry, they lost us.
They can't find us.

104
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,812
You'll live, Cerkutay.

105
00:19:42,916 --> 00:19:45,896
Cerkutay doesn't die.

106
00:19:47,433 --> 00:19:51,513
- I am really happy to see you.
- Sshhh! Silent!

107
00:19:51,521 --> 00:19:55,141
- Aygül Stop!
- Why would you stop me?

108
00:20:00,079 --> 00:20:01,879
Come here.

109
00:20:11,579 --> 00:20:16,189
Let him be alive. He'll take us to
Togay.

110
00:20:26,965 --> 00:20:30,575
What I am saying is that I'll not
come here for a while.

111
00:20:31,754 --> 00:20:34,414
I need to step back.

112
00:20:35,694 --> 00:20:39,504
You proved yourself to Osman already.

113
00:20:39,707 --> 00:20:42,287
What makes you step back?

114
00:20:42,559 --> 00:20:44,694
I am the one whose life is in danger.

115
00:20:44,694 --> 00:20:48,654
Are you afriad of someone whose dignity
is vanishing step by step?

116
00:20:51,117 --> 00:20:55,405
Lord Nicola returned from
Emperor's castle.

117
00:20:55,405 --> 00:20:59,415
So Emperor still trusts him.

118
00:21:00,827 --> 00:21:03,252
He must be stronger now.

119
00:21:03,252 --> 00:21:06,952
Both stronger and more crowded.

120
00:21:08,009 --> 00:21:12,889
To finish Osman, Nicola now sees
Togay.

121
00:21:14,305 --> 00:21:21,155
Osman's enemies have never been
united that well before.

122
00:21:21,197 --> 00:21:26,777
And you have never been closer to
the post, Dündar Bey.

123
00:21:28,168 --> 00:21:32,608
Do you understand that you should
no longer be afraid, Dündar Bey?

124
00:21:49,220 --> 00:21:51,550
Can I come in, my Bey?

125
00:21:53,386 --> 00:21:55,346
Come.

126
00:21:59,816 --> 00:22:01,946
My Bey, Cerkutay and Aygül are back.

127
00:22:08,131 --> 00:22:11,391
They brought a Mongol.

128
00:22:20,518 --> 00:22:23,318
How has Nicola changed?

129
00:22:23,327 --> 00:22:26,397
You'll see yourself now.

130
00:22:32,308 --> 00:22:37,898
He returned from Constantinie with
the strenght you cannot even imagine.

131
00:22:39,072 --> 00:22:41,172
What does he want?

132
00:22:41,510 --> 00:22:45,340
He couldn't accept Flatyos' death.

133
00:22:45,963 --> 00:22:49,533
Do not dare to bother him.

134
00:23:49,939 --> 00:23:52,819
Be ready to die, Aris.

135
00:23:56,094 --> 00:24:01,414
I am always ready to die for the
empire, for you Nicola.

136
00:24:15,517 --> 00:24:22,387
All the Lords are going to be ready for
a final attack.

137
00:24:22,546 --> 00:24:28,626
We'll take Sogut to break Osman.

138
00:24:32,121 --> 00:24:34,931
Do we have soldiers for that, Nicola?

139
00:24:45,833 --> 00:24:50,863
Do you want death now or when
Osman's sword hit you, huh?

140
00:25:13,915 --> 00:25:16,695
I want to die in the battle, Nicola.

141
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:25,450
Osman gathered the Beys.

142
00:25:25,498 --> 00:25:30,428
He wants Inegol.
Tell me, Aris.

143
00:25:30,864 --> 00:25:38,054
If Osman conquers Inegol, how and where
are you going to live?

144
00:25:39,379 --> 00:25:43,659
You'll be sitting in your castle
like bumblebees.

145
00:25:43,743 --> 00:25:47,293
You wouldn't want that, would you?

146
00:25:48,977 --> 00:25:52,147
I am ready to die for you, Nicola.

147
00:25:54,173 --> 00:26:00,193
Then you should listen to me
real carefully.

148
00:26:02,692 --> 00:26:09,962
While Osman is planning to take Inegol,
we'll hit him in Sogut.

149
00:26:11,377 --> 00:26:15,751
Emperor will send a huge army.

150
00:26:15,751 --> 00:26:21,431
The fearful commander Kolonos will
be leading them.

151
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:29,200
So the Turks will end finally,
right Nicola?

152
00:26:29,587 --> 00:26:32,047
May Jesus protect our Empire.

153
00:26:35,573 --> 00:26:40,633
Jesus couldn't even protected himself
from Rome!

154
00:26:55,375 --> 00:27:04,085
Dear Helen, finally it's time to meet
Geyhatu's hunter dog Black Shaman Togay.

155
00:27:04,897 --> 00:27:07,697
He departed, sir.

156
00:27:12,353 --> 00:27:21,293
And you Aris, see all the Lords
and tell them to get their armies ready.

157
00:27:51,005 --> 00:27:54,095
Talk, where is Togay?

158
00:28:09,113 --> 00:28:12,853
So that's it, huh?

159
00:28:15,089 --> 00:28:17,469
You are going to talk.

160
00:28:49,303 --> 00:28:50,813
Cerkutay.

161
00:29:18,667 --> 00:29:20,547
You are going to talk.

162
00:29:22,693 --> 00:29:25,033
You are going to talk.

163
00:29:29,441 --> 00:29:32,171
You are going to talk.

164
00:29:40,774 --> 00:29:42,524
Where is Togay?

165
00:30:47,741 --> 00:30:53,411
Talk, where is that ignoble who wounded
my father, killed my alps?

166
00:30:53,603 --> 00:30:55,303
Talk!

167
00:30:55,470 --> 00:31:04,110
Togay is now you shade.
He'll be after you until he kills you.

168
00:31:05,793 --> 00:31:07,773
Malhun Hatun!

169
00:31:08,104 --> 00:31:10,614
I need him alive.

170
00:31:15,147 --> 00:31:17,577
I have to talk to you.

171
00:31:23,074 --> 00:31:29,514
You keep going. If this one dies or
escpaes...

172
00:31:29,971 --> 00:31:34,601
then you'll witness my wrath.

173
00:32:01,727 --> 00:32:04,687
You promised me not to act by yourself.

174
00:32:05,024 --> 00:32:08,271
But you didn't keep your word
and went after Togay!

175
00:32:08,271 --> 00:32:10,921
You left me no choice, Osman Bey.

176
00:32:10,978 --> 00:32:14,948
You tried to hide it even though you knew
it was Togay who attacked.

177
00:32:17,338 --> 00:32:20,828
I was trying to protect you.

178
00:32:28,570 --> 00:32:32,980
The past is past, Osman Bey. We both
want Togay.

179
00:32:33,455 --> 00:32:36,915
We should find out how we
are going to find him.

180
00:32:40,175 --> 00:32:46,975
First of all, we need to
lodge your father.

181
00:32:48,765 --> 00:32:51,695
The right thing is to be together.

182
00:32:55,224 --> 00:33:01,564
If that dog doesn't talk, what is
your plan than?

183
00:33:02,807 --> 00:33:05,727
I'll pour water to scorpion's nest.

184
00:33:06,011 --> 00:33:08,331
He'll come out.

185
00:34:16,643 --> 00:34:19,203
What are you going to give me, Nicola?

186
00:34:25,460 --> 00:34:30,200
The drink I made for Geyhatu
when he came.

187
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:32,523
Kumis.

188
00:34:43,419 --> 00:34:48,479
To Togay who shot Osman in heart.

189
00:35:30,122 --> 00:35:34,142
Are you showing me respect because you
fear me or...

190
00:35:35,402 --> 00:35:38,112
do you fear Osman?

191
00:35:38,270 --> 00:35:42,980
What I am afraid of is that Osman may
trample your dead body.

192
00:35:50,169 --> 00:35:55,109
Save your anger to Osman, not me.

193
00:35:57,193 --> 00:36:00,053
My anger is enough for both of you.

194
00:36:05,488 --> 00:36:12,858
Shooting him in middle of a meeting
doesn't make you hero, Togay.

195
00:36:14,515 --> 00:36:23,635
My castle, my soldiers, and my spies
will be under your command...

196
00:36:25,421 --> 00:36:27,711
with a single command of mine...

197
00:36:32,745 --> 00:36:35,475
like I did help to Geyhatu.

198
00:36:47,503 --> 00:36:50,143
Will you give your throne to me?

199
00:37:01,118 --> 00:37:09,848
As long as Osman lives, this throne is no
use for neither me nor you, Togay.

200
00:37:17,343 --> 00:37:22,613
In return of the soldiers you'll give me..

201
00:37:24,421 --> 00:37:29,141
I'll let you live in this stone grave.

202
00:37:35,115 --> 00:37:39,995
- Make your mind.
- You'll come back.

203
00:37:42,131 --> 00:37:44,861
You'll come back.

204
00:37:54,016 --> 00:37:57,116
You'll come back.

205
00:37:57,637 --> 00:37:59,567
You barbaric.

206
00:38:37,208 --> 00:38:40,798
My brother, help!

207
00:38:43,115 --> 00:38:45,295
You'll live Cerkutay.

208
00:38:47,007 --> 00:38:49,797
You saved my life.

209
00:39:10,261 --> 00:39:12,151
What is wrong with you?

210
00:39:12,721 --> 00:39:16,291
There's something going on since
we captuerd that Mongol.

211
00:39:19,488 --> 00:39:23,278
I remembered my childhood while tracking.

212
00:39:25,088 --> 00:39:27,368
The days I lived in forest.

213
00:39:27,935 --> 00:39:30,415
Is it your childhood or...

214
00:39:30,989 --> 00:39:34,139
the days you fought for Balgay.

215
00:39:42,545 --> 00:39:46,025
Why are you silent?

216
00:39:46,726 --> 00:39:49,056
I was raised by jackals, Aygül.

217
00:39:56,269 --> 00:39:59,329
Jackals are summoning me.

218
00:40:00,344 --> 00:40:02,544
The forest is calling me.

219
00:40:02,841 --> 00:40:07,281
I hear voices they say
"Come to us, Cerkutay"

220
00:40:10,435 --> 00:40:12,585
Are you going to live?

221
00:40:18,679 --> 00:40:22,319
Even if they think I trciked them all...

222
00:40:23,336 --> 00:40:28,676
You should know that I would never
trick Bamsı Bey.

223
00:40:30,609 --> 00:40:32,849
What does that mean?

224
00:40:39,772 --> 00:40:46,262
When moon lights on my sword's steel,
it shines like your eyes.

225
00:40:47,345 --> 00:40:48,615
But...

226
00:40:50,408 --> 00:40:51,938
But?

227
00:40:53,439 --> 00:40:57,439
Cerkutay missed the forest.

228
00:41:17,632 --> 00:41:19,512
Leave then!

229
00:41:51,508 --> 00:41:54,468
How can you go after Togay without
my command?

230
00:41:54,934 --> 00:41:56,924
I am not dead yet, daughter!

231
00:41:58,137 --> 00:42:01,117
You were not in a condition to make call,
my Bey.

232
00:42:07,923 --> 00:42:12,533
How did you allow that?

233
00:42:13,125 --> 00:42:18,295
My beloved daughter goes after that
dirty dog...

234
00:42:18,461 --> 00:42:21,371
and you don't stop her, right?

235
00:42:21,702 --> 00:42:26,612
They are sinless.
They obeyed me.

236
00:42:29,762 --> 00:42:35,312
If Osman Bey didn't hide the fact that he
was after Togay, I wouldn't do this.

237
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:43,012
I doubt Osman Bey knows what to hide.

238
00:42:44,754 --> 00:42:48,204
Is there anything about Togay?

239
00:42:48,810 --> 00:42:52,930
One of Osman Bey's alps captured their
man, my Bey.

240
00:42:55,537 --> 00:42:57,637
He hasn't talked yet, my Bey.

241
00:42:58,067 --> 00:43:01,307
He'll, he will.

242
00:43:01,345 --> 00:43:08,985
Everyone talks if you know where to hit.

243
00:43:12,643 --> 00:43:16,653
Arrange accomodation for
our Alps to come.

244
00:43:17,699 --> 00:43:22,289
Take care of them. Bring the
rest of the alps to me.

245
00:43:23,183 --> 00:43:25,033
Yes my Bey.

246
00:43:25,808 --> 00:43:29,548
We'll do our job ourselves.

247
00:43:34,953 --> 00:43:37,393
- Alaca Hatun.
- Yes my Bey.

248
00:43:38,013 --> 00:43:41,696
You'll be my eyes and ears.

249
00:43:41,696 --> 00:43:44,756
Don't worry, my Bey. I'll have my eyes
wide open.

250
00:43:47,226 --> 00:43:51,116
I'll be alone with my daughter now.

251
00:44:29,904 --> 00:44:36,694
The one who killed the captive whom Osman
tried to make talk and who told enemies

252
00:44:37,186 --> 00:44:41,456
about the meeting and shed our blood is
the one whose finger fits in this ring.

253
00:44:45,796 --> 00:44:48,226
You did a good job to hide this.

254
00:44:50,105 --> 00:44:54,745
If it's Osman's close ones, Osman may
show mercy.

255
00:44:54,928 --> 00:44:58,718
But if we found him before he does,
we'll make it right.

256
00:44:58,908 --> 00:45:01,588
we'll make it right.

257
00:45:02,875 --> 00:45:05,745
Is there anything about the owner of
this ring?

258
00:45:20,535 --> 00:45:22,125
Dündar Bey.

259
00:45:25,976 --> 00:45:30,744
Dündar Bey, why are you wandering?

260
00:45:30,744 --> 00:45:33,473
You are wearing off the rugs.

261
00:45:33,473 --> 00:45:38,593
They have never been stronger, Hatun.

262
00:45:38,612 --> 00:45:43,152
Osman's enemies have never been stronger.

263
00:45:45,562 --> 00:45:49,732
Damaging him inside and outside, huh?

264
00:45:49,732 --> 00:45:52,082
What do you mean by inside?

265
00:45:53,807 --> 00:45:57,467
When a Hatun is disturbed by someone or
something...

266
00:45:58,051 --> 00:46:02,791
her man is the real one who will suffer
the consequences.

267
00:46:02,971 --> 00:46:08,271
That man of hers cannot be happy
until she gets happy.

268
00:46:11,790 --> 00:46:18,944
Malhun Hatun seems to bother Bala Hatun
very much.

269
00:46:19,244 --> 00:46:21,974
I know it like the back of my hand...

270
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:30,213
that she waited Malhun Hatun to die
in the tent today.

271
00:46:33,252 --> 00:46:37,532
You are mistaken, Hatun.
This is Bala Hatun.

272
00:46:37,553 --> 00:46:40,813
So what?
She is a she.

273
00:46:42,100 --> 00:46:45,960
A Hatun is a Hatun.

274
00:46:47,725 --> 00:46:54,115
You are talking to an expert.

275
00:46:58,992 --> 00:47:03,582
You have plans, apparently.

276
00:47:03,582 --> 00:47:08,342
Good then.
Good, good.

277
00:47:11,609 --> 00:47:13,659
Can I, Umur Bey?

278
00:47:14,384 --> 00:47:16,514
Come Osman Bey.

279
00:47:29,525 --> 00:47:31,675
We have been honored Osman Bey.

280
00:47:32,742 --> 00:47:35,842
You are the guests here.

281
00:47:35,937 --> 00:47:38,357
We have been honored.

282
00:47:41,370 --> 00:47:43,650
Here, Osman Bey.

283
00:47:51,746 --> 00:47:54,176
I hope you don't need anything.

284
00:47:54,659 --> 00:47:57,809
We don't, we have everything.

285
00:47:57,813 --> 00:48:00,608
We have been well hosted,
Eyvallah. (thanks)

286
00:48:00,608 --> 00:48:02,038
Eyvallah (you are welcome.)

287
00:48:02,780 --> 00:48:10,580
We are tired of waiting for your words
about the dog who shed our blood, Osman Bey.

288
00:48:19,007 --> 00:48:21,227
Don't worry.

289
00:48:23,439 --> 00:48:29,589
I'll bring Togay's and his soldiers'
heads to you one by one.

290
00:48:30,520 --> 00:48:33,679
Do you have a plan, Osman Bey?

291
00:48:33,679 --> 00:48:39,929
Of course I do, a plan
that will shed blood.

292
00:48:39,965 --> 00:48:43,375
When, Osman Bey?

293
00:48:44,281 --> 00:48:48,426
We accepted your invitation,
came by here.

294
00:48:48,426 --> 00:48:52,233
We almost died?
When?

295
00:48:57,573 --> 00:48:59,883
We are responsible for what happened.

296
00:49:00,898 --> 00:49:05,198
But don't worry about that.

297
00:49:06,180 --> 00:49:09,960
We don't worry about ourselves, Osman Bey.

298
00:49:10,165 --> 00:49:12,865
We worry about the future of our tribe.

299
00:49:12,935 --> 00:49:18,405
We do not fight for ourselves.
We fight for our community.

300
00:49:22,018 --> 00:49:28,708
You hold your head straight against
Geyhatu, you respect our traditions.

301
00:49:30,822 --> 00:49:32,162
But...

302
00:49:35,464 --> 00:49:41,804
You saw what happened when Malhun Hatun
acted herself.

303
00:49:49,081 --> 00:49:56,911
I do not consent to do things
without notifying me.

304
00:50:07,285 --> 00:50:11,065
- Let me leave
- Your lands...

305
00:50:11,816 --> 00:50:14,176
Your invitation.

306
00:50:15,563 --> 00:50:21,322
But this is my tribe, my people,
Osman Bey.

307
00:50:45,892 --> 00:50:51,022
Malhun Hatun, don't leave your father
alone.

308
00:50:56,861 --> 00:50:59,481
Stay with him.

309
00:52:35,935 --> 00:52:37,455
Bala...

310
00:52:47,860 --> 00:52:49,750
I dozed off.

311
00:53:04,733 --> 00:53:06,943
You got tired, didn't you?

312
00:53:10,915 --> 00:53:13,845
May Allah bless you my Bala.

313
00:53:16,129 --> 00:53:18,929
May Allah bless you.

314
00:53:24,180 --> 00:53:27,780
You hosted our guests very well...

315
00:53:29,536 --> 00:53:32,826
like how we were supposed to do.

316
00:53:34,076 --> 00:53:38,136
I am happy if they are happy.

317
00:53:38,309 --> 00:53:40,369
Oh, my Bala, oh.

318
00:53:42,218 --> 00:53:44,858
We are getting through difficult days.

319
00:53:45,371 --> 00:53:53,841
A Kayı Bey and a Kayı Hatun goes
from one difficulty to another.

320
00:53:55,996 --> 00:53:57,586
My Bala.

321
00:54:00,280 --> 00:54:08,070
Do not think that I am angry at you,
accuse you just because...

322
00:54:08,412 --> 00:54:10,262
I am angry at that time.

323
00:54:15,165 --> 00:54:21,195
My Bala, I want something else from you.

324
00:54:24,565 --> 00:54:26,855
Of course my Bey.

325
00:54:31,738 --> 00:54:34,438
You need to feel them, my Bala.

326
00:54:34,457 --> 00:54:38,987
They accepted our invitation, they
migrated here.

327
00:54:40,439 --> 00:54:42,559
They are waiting for a homeland.

328
00:54:44,128 --> 00:54:47,218
And they are already in the target
of our enemies.

329
00:54:48,927 --> 00:54:52,907
Of course they will suspect.

330
00:54:52,907 --> 00:54:55,977
Of course they will want to
interfere in our things.

331
00:54:59,033 --> 00:55:04,453
My Bala, we are the founder ones.

332
00:55:05,412 --> 00:55:07,902
We are the ones that gather people.

333
00:55:08,888 --> 00:55:13,918
We need to be levelheaded.

334
00:55:15,770 --> 00:55:19,470
We will be patient.

335
00:55:19,810 --> 00:55:21,870
We will put up with them.

336
00:55:22,749 --> 00:55:27,149
And we will get rid of the dark clouds
above Kayı Tribe.

337
00:55:27,784 --> 00:55:32,604
We'll spread our light to everywhere.

338
00:55:35,342 --> 00:55:37,062
My Bala.

339
00:55:39,411 --> 00:55:41,271
My Bala?

340
00:55:48,644 --> 00:55:51,194
Hey, rose.

341
00:55:53,941 --> 00:55:56,201
You are secured in my arms.

342
00:55:59,176 --> 00:56:02,016
Sleep here.

343
00:56:04,713 --> 00:56:07,103
Osman is watching for you.

344
00:56:57,960 --> 00:57:02,790
I am here to pay back.

345
00:57:28,929 --> 00:57:30,819
Be quick.

346
00:57:44,649 --> 00:57:47,259
I knew you were still a Mongol.

347
00:57:47,259 --> 00:57:50,209
Cut it!

348
00:57:59,803 --> 00:58:04,263
It's my duty to call Cerkutay to account..

349
00:58:04,761 --> 00:58:09,341
just like how he tricked me, my Bey.

350
00:58:13,305 --> 00:58:15,715
He tricked us all.

351
00:58:20,731 --> 00:58:22,621
All of us.

352
00:58:25,625 --> 00:58:27,925
We wanted to believe, Osman Bey.

353
00:58:28,078 --> 00:58:33,508
We wanted to believe that he repented,
that he'd continue living like a Turk.

354
00:58:36,164 --> 00:58:39,174
Bamsı Bey, that's why we were deceived.

355
00:58:50,157 --> 00:58:56,637
So that was why infidels knew every
step of ours.

356
00:58:56,783 --> 00:59:00,873
We gave martyrs because of that betrayer,
my Bey!

357
00:59:07,919 --> 00:59:12,949
Did you spot him through?
Are you sure it was Cerkutay?

358
00:59:13,469 --> 00:59:19,689
Bamsı Bey, I wouldn't give his name if
I was not sure.

359
00:59:30,788 --> 00:59:33,968
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come!

360
00:59:41,224 --> 00:59:43,764
Are you sure, Gencebey?

361
00:59:49,739 --> 00:59:54,799
Tell me, Aygül.
Was he suspicious?

362
00:59:59,063 --> 01:00:02,523
I was raised by jackals, Aygül.
The forest is calling for me.

363
01:00:03,114 --> 01:00:07,854
I hear voices they say
"Cerkutay come to us"

364
01:00:09,657 --> 01:00:12,637
Cerkutay missed the forest.

365
01:00:13,042 --> 01:00:15,992
He spoke to me like
taking a farewell.

366
01:00:21,673 --> 01:00:24,223
What did he say, daughter?

367
01:00:29,891 --> 01:00:35,981
They may think that I tricked everyone,
but I would never trick Bamsı Bey, he said.

368
01:00:44,993 --> 01:00:47,713
He really liked you, Bamsı Bey.

369
01:00:52,622 --> 01:00:56,612
Why did he betray?
Why?

370
01:01:05,402 --> 01:01:11,793
The meeting is over.
We'll find and punish him.

371
01:01:14,009 --> 01:01:17,141
My wound is not deep.
I'll come too, my Bey.

372
01:01:17,141 --> 01:01:19,291
I will come too, my Bey.

373
01:01:20,835 --> 01:01:23,225
Can I, my Bey?

374
01:01:25,218 --> 01:01:27,118
Let's go!

375
01:02:13,250 --> 01:02:16,430
You acted like a Mongol, don't be upset.

376
01:02:20,467 --> 01:02:23,277
I finally found home.

377
01:02:24,841 --> 01:02:27,251
Then I betrayed again.

378
01:02:28,257 --> 01:02:30,807
I cannot go back.

379
01:02:31,236 --> 01:02:33,536
Osman Bey would kill me.

380
01:02:33,580 --> 01:02:37,050
It was not your home. Come with me.

381
01:02:37,110 --> 01:02:40,260
To your real home.
Return to Mongols.

382
01:02:40,268 --> 01:02:43,408
Togay will accept a fighter like you.

383
01:02:46,657 --> 01:02:48,667
He'll suspect me.

384
01:02:51,744 --> 01:02:54,974
I'll defend you, tell them you saved me.

385
01:03:00,529 --> 01:03:03,529
Let's go then.

386
01:03:03,579 --> 01:03:05,549
Cerkutay is hungry.

387
01:03:06,569 --> 01:03:09,069
You were always hungry, Cerkutay.

388
01:03:16,908 --> 01:03:19,848
I can't believe how Cerkutay did this
to us.

389
01:03:20,549 --> 01:03:23,319
He made us like him so much.

390
01:03:23,918 --> 01:03:28,788
He was joking around everytime I saw him.

391
01:03:29,093 --> 01:03:32,068
- He was a good friend to Aygül as well.
- True.

392
01:03:32,068 --> 01:03:34,028
She must be devestated.

393
01:03:38,804 --> 01:03:42,084
- Salamun Aleikum
- Aleikum salam.

394
01:03:43,288 --> 01:03:45,298
Alaikum salam.

395
01:03:45,573 --> 01:03:47,783
I am searching for Osman Bey.

396
01:03:48,289 --> 01:03:50,699
He is not in the tent.

397
01:03:52,354 --> 01:03:55,377
Okay.
I'll check that Mongol dog.

398
01:03:55,377 --> 01:03:57,207
Stop, Hatun.

399
01:03:59,848 --> 01:04:01,808
What is it, Bala Hatun?

400
01:04:04,689 --> 01:04:09,559
You tell me, Malhun Hatun.
You are acting by yourself again.

401
01:04:15,918 --> 01:04:21,368
The only one who knows where Togay is
is the dog who you cannot make talk.

402
01:04:22,870 --> 01:04:27,720
Now let me make that dog talk.
The thing you cannot do.

403
01:04:35,828 --> 01:04:39,068
What is it? Is there something wrong?

404
01:04:43,523 --> 01:04:45,783
That dog went off.

405
01:04:46,880 --> 01:04:49,610
What are you talking about Hatun?

406
01:04:50,461 --> 01:04:53,801
Step back while you are looking
dead in my eye!

407
01:04:54,461 --> 01:04:57,911
I'd look at Osman Bey's eyes
if he were here.

408
01:05:00,076 --> 01:05:03,306
You couldn't take care of a dog!

409
01:06:12,713 --> 01:06:17,023
Tell me.
Who is this dog?

410
01:06:17,636 --> 01:06:19,886
How did you got out?

411
01:06:21,208 --> 01:06:24,448
My blood brother Cerkutay saved me
from Osman's cage.

412
01:06:29,862 --> 01:06:31,592
Tell me.

413
01:06:32,123 --> 01:06:36,613
I am Balgay's commander Cerkutay.

414
01:06:36,882 --> 01:06:41,562
Balgay is dead.
Why are you alive?

415
01:06:42,428 --> 01:06:49,337
I didn't give my soul to Erlik Khan to
take revenge from Osman.

416
01:06:50,187 --> 01:06:54,177
- Tell me.
- I obeyed Osman.

417
01:06:54,785 --> 01:06:56,915
I tricked him.

418
01:06:57,475 --> 01:06:59,695
Why now?

419
01:07:00,626 --> 01:07:03,406
Black Shaman Togay is back.

420
01:07:04,190 --> 01:07:07,200
I came back to fight with him.

421
01:07:09,345 --> 01:07:12,865
What do you offer to Togay, Cerkutay?

422
01:07:13,702 --> 01:07:18,442
Geyhatu's two huge enemy will unite.
I know where Umur Bey is setting tents.

423
01:07:18,658 --> 01:07:22,748
If we don't raid them now, they'll
get bigger.

424
01:07:33,558 --> 01:07:36,788
The smell of treason.

425
01:08:01,730 --> 01:08:05,840
The goat smell on you outsmell the
smell of treason!

426
01:08:08,159 --> 01:08:10,569
Why would I believe you?

427
01:08:16,292 --> 01:08:22,452
I didn't sell myself to Osman!

428
01:08:22,560 --> 01:08:26,982
I will save Göktuğ like I did Suci.

429
01:08:26,982 --> 01:08:29,572
Give me a chance, Togay.

430
01:08:44,316 --> 01:08:49,752
Stake him on the arms!
If he lies, cut his tongue!

431
01:08:49,942 --> 01:08:52,412
Cut his head off his body!

432
01:08:53,486 --> 01:08:58,846
Give his body to ravens,
give his soul to Erlik Khan!

433
01:09:00,210 --> 01:09:12,750
Time to shed blood!

434
01:10:13,322 --> 01:10:17,772
Sir, Cerkutay was right. There are tents,
they are just setting up.

435
01:10:26,257 --> 01:10:28,207
Let's go!

436
01:12:20,774 --> 01:12:22,774
Ya Allah!

437
01:13:14,901 --> 01:13:17,791
Allah is eternal!

438
01:13:41,816 --> 01:13:43,656
Allah is eternal!

439
01:13:54,010 --> 01:13:57,170
- Cerkutay!
- Mad girl, what are you doing here?

440
01:14:00,874 --> 01:14:03,274
I thought you'd die!

441
01:14:08,130 --> 01:14:13,560
Cerkutay does not die.
Cerkutay does not die.

442
01:14:17,824 --> 01:14:19,874
Let's go!

443
01:14:23,103 --> 01:14:24,353
Let's go!

444
01:16:42,517 --> 01:16:45,337
Ertugrul Ghazi's son Gokboru.

445
01:16:48,906 --> 01:16:51,646
Where is your master Togay?

446
01:16:52,654 --> 01:16:55,504
Come here Turk.

447
01:17:35,336 --> 01:17:38,026
My Bey, we killed all of the soldiers.

448
01:17:38,147 --> 01:17:40,777
I left one wounded as you said.

449
01:17:42,863 --> 01:17:48,773
When that soldiers goes back to Togay,
he'll want to come back stronger.

450
01:17:49,486 --> 01:17:51,786
He'll get help from Nicola.

451
01:17:59,148 --> 01:18:01,858
Cerkutay!

452
01:18:05,145 --> 01:18:07,535
You did well, Cerkutay.

453
01:18:08,994 --> 01:18:10,435
Eyvallah my Bey.

454
01:18:10,435 --> 01:18:12,836
I wish I was dead instead of...

455
01:18:15,226 --> 01:18:17,376
saving him, my Bey

456
01:18:19,873 --> 01:18:23,013
They say betrayal is though...

457
01:18:24,048 --> 01:18:26,018
I now know it.

458
01:18:31,311 --> 01:18:36,591
Then you should save your brother,
Cerkutay.

459
01:18:38,465 --> 01:18:42,825
That way, you'll have no debt left.

460
01:18:53,681 --> 01:18:56,891
- Are you fine, my Bey?
- I am fine.

461
01:18:58,286 --> 01:19:00,216
I am fine.

462
01:19:03,901 --> 01:19:06,971
Why did Boke call me Gokboru?

463
01:19:09,423 --> 01:19:11,593
I was thinking about that.

464
01:19:15,144 --> 01:19:19,834
He showed his souls your blood, my Bey.

465
01:20:29,143 --> 01:20:33,293
Gokboru bit us.

466
01:20:35,069 --> 01:20:37,339
We got ambushed.

467
01:20:39,112 --> 01:20:44,092
We shall mount up.
We have no place for weaks.

468
01:21:03,400 --> 01:21:07,720
- Can I come in Umur Bey?
- Come, Osman Bey.

469
01:21:17,929 --> 01:21:20,139
Is there something?

470
01:21:20,309 --> 01:21:23,619
Did you find that soldier you failed
to keep possession of?

471
01:21:25,420 --> 01:21:32,420
Osman Bey, I believe in your good deeds.
I have no doubts.

472
01:21:32,690 --> 01:21:39,122
But, forgive me. I think there are
uncommitted things going on in this tent.

473
01:21:39,418 --> 01:21:45,568
How can a captive can run away?

474
01:21:45,873 --> 01:21:53,273
You are right, Umur bey. Obviously,
someone helped him.

475
01:21:53,300 --> 01:21:59,160
We know it, Osman Bey. It was the Mongol
soldier you took in your tent.

476
01:22:07,179 --> 01:22:09,619
Was that a part of your plan?

477
01:22:14,226 --> 01:22:16,206
Eyvallah Osman Bey.

478
01:22:16,881 --> 01:22:21,381
So, what did you get out of this plan?

479
01:22:21,631 --> 01:22:24,371
We cornered Togay.

480
01:22:24,650 --> 01:22:29,344
- What did you get?
- We killed his soldiers.

481
01:22:29,344 --> 01:22:33,724
- What about Togay?
- He didn't take the bait.

482
01:22:33,821 --> 01:22:38,811
If you notified us, we'd find
and take his head, Osman Bey.

483
01:22:40,081 --> 01:22:43,971
There are two rules in this land.

484
01:22:45,650 --> 01:22:51,610
The careless dies in the path of battle.

485
01:22:56,125 --> 01:23:00,135
And the ones who fights Kayı...

486
01:23:03,389 --> 01:23:05,319
die under our swords.

487
01:23:07,375 --> 01:23:09,725
Everybody will learn that...

488
01:23:10,470 --> 01:23:12,780
they shouldn't be hostile against Kayı.

489
01:23:13,042 --> 01:23:17,042
Both our friends and enemies.

490
01:23:43,168 --> 01:23:45,278
I want to know...

491
01:23:45,640 --> 01:23:48,520
everything about Malhun Hatun.

492
01:23:49,108 --> 01:23:51,068
Your command, my Bey.

493
01:23:53,452 --> 01:23:58,862
He doesn't want to include us.

494
01:23:59,188 --> 01:24:01,098
What will we do?

495
01:24:02,963 --> 01:24:07,733
We'll find out where Togay is.

496
01:24:08,751 --> 01:24:11,471
Then I know what to do.

497
01:24:36,755 --> 01:24:39,625
- Speaks in Greek -

498
01:24:45,577 --> 01:24:49,887
- Speaks in Greek -

499
01:24:52,777 --> 01:24:56,277
Until all of the Turks die...

500
01:25:06,657 --> 01:25:09,577
We don't need anyone.

501
01:25:12,059 --> 01:25:14,789
Your soldiers do, sir.

502
01:25:18,432 --> 01:25:20,682
The soldiers are anxious.

503
01:25:20,711 --> 01:25:25,721
They think we're like this because you
don't go to church and beg Jesus.

504
01:25:43,741 --> 01:25:47,891
Only a shepherd needs a herd.

505
01:25:47,930 --> 01:25:51,930
I'm the owner of this herd!

506
01:25:54,518 --> 01:25:56,828
The real owner of the herd...

507
01:25:56,879 --> 01:26:02,689
we will lose if you don't beg Jesus.

508
01:26:05,080 --> 01:26:08,860
Your God already left us.

509
01:26:19,159 --> 01:26:21,299
Sir!

510
01:26:22,334 --> 01:26:26,334
Do you want to lose
the war before it begins?

511
01:26:26,385 --> 01:26:31,515
Don't! If you kill the priest, we won't
have anyone to fight with us!

512
01:26:35,271 --> 01:26:37,901
Togay is back.

513
01:26:40,083 --> 01:26:44,873
You did it, sir!
You did it!

514
01:26:55,216 --> 01:26:57,756
I knew he was.

515
01:26:59,344 --> 01:27:01,184
I knew.

516
01:27:06,916 --> 01:27:09,566
Get out.

517
01:27:19,620 --> 01:27:22,450
I said you would come.

518
01:27:23,404 --> 01:27:27,404
I said you would come for Osman.

519
01:27:45,335 --> 01:27:50,925
I'm sorry for your soldiers by the way.

520
01:27:54,695 --> 01:27:57,805
The soldiers' spirits are with me.

521
01:28:00,599 --> 01:28:04,319
I don't know where
the hell are they but...

522
01:28:04,319 --> 01:28:08,389
Osman's breath is behind you.

523
01:28:08,832 --> 01:28:11,692
I proposed you an agreement.

524
01:28:11,829 --> 01:28:15,339
You refused it. So?
Your soldiers are dead.

525
01:28:15,444 --> 01:28:18,494
Then you came back. However, it's
too late.

526
01:28:19,463 --> 01:28:22,893
You refused my proposal.

527
01:28:24,425 --> 01:28:28,955
Tell me now, Togay.

528
01:28:31,055 --> 01:28:34,265
What do yoı have for me?

529
01:28:36,542 --> 01:28:38,422
I'll give you Söğüt.

530
01:28:45,086 --> 01:28:47,606
How?

531
01:29:05,583 --> 01:29:10,193
Petrus dug tunnels under the Söğüt.

532
01:29:12,703 --> 01:29:20,823
So, you harmed Umur Bey via these tunnels.

533
01:29:27,955 --> 01:29:30,855
I knew...

534
01:29:32,985 --> 01:29:36,425
we would deal sooner or later.

535
01:29:47,896 --> 01:29:52,106
May your war be holy, Osman Bey.
You killed Togay's soldiers.

536
01:29:52,667 --> 01:29:54,837
Thank you, brother.

537
01:29:55,439 --> 01:29:59,819
However, I won't feel comfortable
until I kill him.

538
01:29:59,967 --> 01:30:03,967
- You will do it too.
- Inshallah.

539
01:30:05,283 --> 01:30:09,373
However, you didn't tell
us about the trick you played.

540
01:30:18,662 --> 01:30:21,552
The Beys hide some things, brother.

541
01:30:22,230 --> 01:30:26,620
We don't tell everything.

542
01:30:26,664 --> 01:30:28,984
Yes.

543
01:30:29,614 --> 01:30:32,564
You had to believe in Cerkutay's
betrayal so that...

544
01:30:33,706 --> 01:30:38,776
the traitors wouldn't suspect us.

545
01:30:40,675 --> 01:30:43,295
Cerkutay.

546
01:30:44,767 --> 01:30:47,547
So, you deceived us.

547
01:30:48,059 --> 01:30:52,579
My Osman Bey commanded me, so I did it.

548
01:30:53,826 --> 01:30:56,606
How did you believe anyway, my Bey?

549
01:31:06,825 --> 01:31:10,265
Cerkutay, get some rest.

550
01:31:16,752 --> 01:31:20,352
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come in.

551
01:31:54,249 --> 01:31:57,189
Summon Dündar Bey.

552
01:32:00,538 --> 01:32:03,098
It's about something important.

553
01:32:08,033 --> 01:32:10,893
- We have news from Togay.
- Tell me.

554
01:32:11,086 --> 01:32:15,046
- Togay arrived Nikola's castle.
- İnegöl?

555
01:32:16,321 --> 01:32:19,511
Let me go to İnegöl, father.

556
01:32:19,612 --> 01:32:23,372
So that I will ask for Togay.

557
01:32:30,066 --> 01:32:32,936
Nikola is back from Constantine.

558
01:32:33,594 --> 01:32:38,174
The Emperor promised
him support, obviously.

559
01:32:38,429 --> 01:32:42,169
He'll collect the lords.

560
01:32:44,121 --> 01:32:48,851
Tell us what you think, Osman Bey.

561
01:32:51,043 --> 01:32:56,443
Togay went to see Nikola.

562
01:32:59,253 --> 01:33:05,003
So, they are together in this.

563
01:33:07,521 --> 01:33:12,941
He wants to attack us, Osman Bey.

564
01:33:13,686 --> 01:33:17,166
We should attack them before they do.

565
01:33:17,246 --> 01:33:19,106
Thank you, brother.

566
01:33:19,849 --> 01:33:22,239
I think the same as you.

567
01:33:23,302 --> 01:33:25,612
I think the same as you.

568
01:33:26,426 --> 01:33:31,526
I want to kill the lords first.

569
01:33:32,962 --> 01:33:35,942
How will we benefit from it, Osman Bey?

570
01:33:37,084 --> 01:33:42,744
I'll start with Aris, Lord of Yarhisar,
who is the most difficult one.

571
01:33:43,512 --> 01:33:47,122
I'll keep him here for sometime and...

572
01:33:47,215 --> 01:33:52,305
spread rumors that we work together.

573
01:33:54,557 --> 01:33:58,247
And Nikola will be left alone.

574
01:33:59,443 --> 01:34:03,443
They will be afraid to work
together and...

575
01:34:04,506 --> 01:34:09,266
we will defeat
the İnegöl Castle, Inshallah.

576
01:34:16,199 --> 01:34:18,219
Inshallah.

577
01:34:20,153 --> 01:34:22,433
Inshallah.

578
01:34:26,473 --> 01:34:30,043
What are we waiting for, father?
Let me deal with this.

579
01:34:32,611 --> 01:34:34,971
It's our problem now.

580
01:34:36,768 --> 01:34:40,868
We will figure this out without
Osman Bey knowing.

581
01:34:42,054 --> 01:34:46,054
If he does things without telling us...

582
01:34:46,215 --> 01:34:48,905
we'll do the same.

583
01:34:49,101 --> 01:34:51,581
What are you thinking, father?

584
01:34:52,621 --> 01:34:54,951
We're both harmed.

585
01:34:57,453 --> 01:35:01,093
We'll ask for Togay.

586
01:35:03,606 --> 01:35:06,226
Forgive me, my Bey...

587
01:35:06,372 --> 01:35:08,752
but why does Nikola give us Togay?

588
01:35:08,874 --> 01:35:12,204
Does he want to make Geyhatu angry?

589
01:35:13,157 --> 01:35:16,247
Firstly, we'll send a messenger.

590
01:35:16,356 --> 01:35:20,356
We'll tell him that if we take Togay, we
won't touch him.

591
01:35:21,122 --> 01:35:25,122
If Osman Bey stands up to Lord Nikola...

592
01:35:25,235 --> 01:35:30,085
then what can a Kızılbeyoğlu do?

593
01:35:30,618 --> 01:35:33,948
If it's about going to İnegöl...

594
01:35:34,108 --> 01:35:36,328
we will.

595
01:35:38,822 --> 01:35:44,642
However, I see that he's
in trouble in the tent.

596
01:35:48,547 --> 01:35:52,547
Go to İnegöl as a messenger.

597
01:35:53,435 --> 01:35:56,335
- Your command, my Bey.
- Father.

598
01:35:56,703 --> 01:35:59,353
I want to go if you let me.

599
01:35:59,441 --> 01:36:03,481
They may do bad things, daughter.

600
01:36:03,565 --> 01:36:08,385
If I am your heir, if you see me
worthy of this...

601
01:36:08,857 --> 01:36:11,327
then let me go.

602
01:36:18,421 --> 01:36:21,141
Bring Alaca with you.

603
01:36:21,730 --> 01:36:26,560
Take some Alps with you.

604
01:36:27,045 --> 01:36:30,445
However, be careful, okay?

605
01:36:32,530 --> 01:36:34,910
It's yours.

606
01:36:51,907 --> 01:36:55,647
So, he'll attack the Lord
of Yarhisar, huh?

607
01:36:56,439 --> 01:36:59,769
Will you tell him?

608
01:36:59,988 --> 01:37:03,068
I won't, Hatun.

609
01:37:03,521 --> 01:37:06,341
Osman began to trust me.

610
01:37:06,508 --> 01:37:09,248
I should be careful.

611
01:37:11,931 --> 01:37:15,381
You won't just wait, right?

612
01:37:15,508 --> 01:37:19,768
I have some plans, Hatun.

613
01:37:48,006 --> 01:37:50,306
Thank you.

614
01:37:52,561 --> 01:37:56,641
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (Ithe name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.)

615
01:37:56,727 --> 01:37:59,577
- No, thank you.
- Drink it.

616
01:37:59,920 --> 01:38:03,510
It's healthy.

617
01:38:07,182 --> 01:38:08,232
Thank you.

618
01:38:11,461 --> 01:38:13,401
Abdurrahman Ghazi...

619
01:38:14,167 --> 01:38:15,917
Davut Bey...

620
01:38:16,964 --> 01:38:20,984
...welcome.
I'm so happy you're here.

621
01:38:21,043 --> 01:38:25,043
It's us who are happy, my Sheikh.

622
01:38:28,636 --> 01:38:31,426
If you have no one to talk to...

623
01:38:32,037 --> 01:38:35,627
even if you talk like a canary, it's
in vain.

624
01:38:36,358 --> 01:38:40,658
You go to wars and fight a lot.

625
01:38:41,189 --> 01:38:44,849
Ahis start working by morning pray...

626
01:38:46,308 --> 01:38:49,658
and try to gain money until dawn.

627
01:38:50,149 --> 01:38:54,269
We just talk.

628
01:38:55,098 --> 01:38:58,868
Not at all, my Sheikh.

629
01:39:00,641 --> 01:39:05,261
Beys fight and...

630
01:39:06,449 --> 01:39:09,469
Ahis talk about it.

631
01:39:09,641 --> 01:39:11,991
What then?

632
01:39:12,747 --> 01:39:14,667
There will be a conquest.

633
01:39:15,893 --> 01:39:21,303
A conquest won't be complete
with just a sword.

634
01:39:23,224 --> 01:39:26,704
Doesn't it mean opening?

635
01:39:27,867 --> 01:39:31,337
Open where?

636
01:39:32,265 --> 01:39:36,965
Open to who? From outside or inside?

637
01:39:38,637 --> 01:39:41,737
The sword opens it from outside.

638
01:39:42,073 --> 01:39:44,613
What will open it from inside?

639
01:39:45,837 --> 01:39:48,617
Having Allah's calling.

640
01:39:50,073 --> 01:39:53,603
The door of a wall is opened with a
sword.

641
01:39:54,373 --> 01:39:57,223
What about the door of a heart?

642
01:39:57,665 --> 01:39:59,555
How will it be opened?

643
01:40:01,930 --> 01:40:08,100
Can someone be a Muslim with a sword
if he doesn't feel like a Muslim?

644
01:40:09,327 --> 01:40:14,197
How can this happen?

645
01:40:14,857 --> 01:40:20,557
Ahi will work, produce and sell.

646
01:40:21,006 --> 01:40:25,006
Ahi will buy, make and do.

647
01:40:26,243 --> 01:40:32,623
They shouldn't cheat while working.

648
01:40:33,044 --> 01:40:37,714
Ahis will thrive what is
taken by the sword.

649
01:40:38,560 --> 01:40:40,800
They will make it prosperous.

650
01:40:41,260 --> 01:40:45,660
When serving the public means
serving to Allah...

651
01:40:45,896 --> 01:40:49,356
then the conquest will be complete.

652
01:40:49,968 --> 01:40:55,308
And Islam will spread in the state.

653
01:40:56,681 --> 01:41:01,031
The state will be complete.

654
01:41:02,476 --> 01:41:08,006
If we have summons from Allah, then
we will know that...

655
01:41:08,499 --> 01:41:14,069
we will get our acts together.

656
01:41:14,424 --> 01:41:18,694
We will be fair to Muslims and...

657
01:41:18,744 --> 01:41:23,614
non- muslims.

658
01:41:24,762 --> 01:41:29,732
If Hasan isn't fair to our neighbors
and everyone...

659
01:41:30,055 --> 01:41:33,815
there won't be a state for us here.

660
01:41:34,763 --> 01:41:40,393
If the blacksmith Davut Bey
can't do self-preservation...

661
01:41:42,428 --> 01:41:45,968
there won't be a state for us here.

662
01:41:48,583 --> 01:41:53,573
We won't be complete until we are fair.

663
01:41:54,514 --> 01:42:00,634
According to some, mushriks from
Mecca were so cruel.

664
01:42:01,427 --> 01:42:05,687
Their cruelty was so harsh that...

665
01:42:06,981 --> 01:42:13,741
everyone was oppressed.

666
01:42:14,944 --> 01:42:17,984
Our Efendi saw that the oppression...

667
01:42:18,193 --> 01:42:22,493
was getting crueler every day...

668
01:42:24,065 --> 01:42:27,035
and He had felt sad.

669
01:42:28,327 --> 01:42:32,327
He decided something to...

670
01:42:32,327 --> 01:42:36,327
rescue his companions.

671
01:42:36,834 --> 01:42:42,404
And he sent the Muslims to
Najashi, King of Habesh.

672
01:42:42,904 --> 01:42:46,904
Najashi was a Christian.

673
01:42:47,145 --> 01:42:53,545
And our Efendi knew that
he was a Christian.

674
01:42:54,599 --> 01:42:56,549
He said that...

675
01:42:56,836 --> 01:43:02,186
"Go to Najashi, he is a fair King."

676
01:43:02,532 --> 01:43:04,672
That's it.

677
01:43:09,182 --> 01:43:10,882
Our Efendi...

678
01:43:11,807 --> 01:43:19,977
didn't care about Najashi being
a Christian, Muslim or Jew.

679
01:43:21,008 --> 01:43:23,718
He said he was fair.

680
01:43:25,402 --> 01:43:30,652
There is no leader for us other
than our Efendi. (Muhammad.)

681
01:43:34,536 --> 01:43:39,776
Then, we will follow our leader...

682
01:43:40,050 --> 01:43:45,060
or we won't and we will be destroyed.

683
01:45:58,516 --> 01:46:00,616
Someone is following us.

684
01:46:00,681 --> 01:46:03,671
No. Stay still.

685
01:46:03,951 --> 01:46:07,111
Now is not the time.
Alaca.

686
01:46:08,125 --> 01:46:09,835
Hide us.

687
01:46:23,226 --> 01:46:25,736
Take off your cloth.

688
01:46:45,517 --> 01:46:47,837
We will go where we will meet alone.

689
01:46:47,958 --> 01:46:51,398
Let's meet there when we get rid
of the man who follows us.

690
01:46:54,340 --> 01:46:55,990
Alaca, be careful.

691
01:46:59,476 --> 01:47:01,316
Let's fall apart.

692
01:47:03,884 --> 01:47:04,894
Come on.

693
01:47:05,608 --> 01:47:06,468
Come on.

694
01:47:41,574 --> 01:47:43,044
This is not good.

695
01:47:44,558 --> 01:47:46,688
This is not good at all.

696
01:48:30,122 --> 01:48:31,732
Alps!

697
01:48:32,971 --> 01:48:34,391
From now on...

698
01:48:35,544 --> 01:48:37,624
Our enemy isn't just one.

699
01:48:39,887 --> 01:48:44,867
Our shields aren't strong as their tricks.

700
01:48:47,156 --> 01:48:51,326
However, we will beat them...

701
01:48:52,334 --> 01:48:53,504
with our minds...

702
01:48:56,739 --> 01:48:59,589
not just with our swords.

703
01:49:05,391 --> 01:49:08,691
We will be together.

704
01:49:09,314 --> 01:49:16,234
We will be one and beat them
like an iron fist.

705
01:49:20,296 --> 01:49:21,936
You...

706
01:49:23,596 --> 01:49:28,066
are my fighter valiants behind me.

707
01:49:31,091 --> 01:49:35,261
We won't feel pity for anyone today.

708
01:49:36,869 --> 01:49:41,269
However, I want the lord alive.

709
01:49:43,676 --> 01:49:47,676
The rest will be killed by your swords.

710
01:49:51,835 --> 01:49:55,565
Alps, come on!

711
01:50:28,547 --> 01:50:31,957
I'm here as the messenger
of my father Umur Bey.

712
01:50:32,619 --> 01:50:38,049
What do you want from me, the
messenger of Umur Bey, Malhun Hatun?

713
01:50:38,340 --> 01:50:42,340
I want Togay, Geyhatu's dog.

714
01:50:46,543 --> 01:50:48,193
What will you...

715
01:50:49,444 --> 01:50:52,214
give me in return for him?

716
01:50:53,380 --> 01:50:56,110
Osman's head?

717
01:50:57,380 --> 01:51:01,310
In return for it, you'll keep your head.

718
01:51:08,710 --> 01:51:09,800
What if...

719
01:51:11,704 --> 01:51:14,924
I don't give Togay?

720
01:51:16,111 --> 01:51:20,531
My father and Osman Bey will
destroy your castle.

721
01:51:21,515 --> 01:51:24,595
You should know that.

722
01:51:46,972 --> 01:51:50,202
It seems you found each other.

723
01:52:22,901 --> 01:52:26,001
Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the most great!)

724
01:52:27,359 --> 01:52:29,729
Protect the lord!

725
01:52:46,016 --> 01:52:48,656
Don't lift your shields down.

726
01:53:08,290 --> 01:53:09,920
Hold on.

727
01:53:10,895 --> 01:53:12,205
Attack!

728
01:53:13,701 --> 01:53:16,641
Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the most great!)

729
01:53:39,527 --> 01:53:41,727
Bring me the lord.

730
01:55:09,984 --> 01:55:11,874
Tie him.

731
01:55:44,968 --> 01:55:47,108
If you...

732
01:55:52,027 --> 01:55:54,497
carry...

733
01:55:57,754 --> 01:55:59,454
rice in the wrong way...

734
01:56:06,350 --> 01:56:08,890
you will...

735
01:56:17,624 --> 01:56:20,264
carry...

736
01:56:22,947 --> 01:56:25,687
soil...

737
01:56:30,328 --> 01:56:32,048
while you're going back.

738
01:56:54,831 --> 01:56:58,831
Sir, Osman caught Lord Aris and
brought him to his tent.

739
01:57:15,151 --> 01:57:17,221
Togay...

740
01:57:23,247 --> 01:57:24,507
"I bear witness that there is
no deity but Allah..."

741
01:57:24,577 --> 01:57:28,137
Togay, don't kill her.

742
01:57:28,529 --> 01:57:31,199
She will give us Osman.

743
01:57:34,219 --> 01:57:37,879
"...and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the messenger of Allah."

744
01:58:37,182 --> 01:58:41,182
My lion! He brings victory every day!

745
01:59:01,552 --> 01:59:03,902
Thank Allah.

746
01:59:05,032 --> 01:59:09,032
- We're getting rid of black clouds.
- Thank Allah.

747
01:59:09,526 --> 01:59:13,776
He brought the Lord of Yarhisar.

748
01:59:14,272 --> 01:59:18,272
No one can stop him, Dündar Bey.

749
01:59:24,974 --> 01:59:27,274
Bring him inside.

750
02:00:17,287 --> 02:00:19,467
What happened?

751
02:00:20,818 --> 02:00:22,358
My Bey...

752
02:00:22,539 --> 02:00:26,609
Malhun Hatun and her Alps
disappeared without a trace.

753
02:00:54,940 --> 02:00:59,030
The blood started to
drop from Osman's sword.

754
02:01:06,808 --> 02:01:10,178
You can go, Boran.

755
02:02:36,326 --> 02:02:38,176
Come.

756
02:02:45,995 --> 02:02:50,515
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (Ithe name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.)

757
02:02:54,295 --> 02:02:56,985
Are you hungry? Eat.

758
02:03:01,018 --> 02:03:02,438
Thank you.

759
02:03:03,279 --> 02:03:05,059
Okay.

760
02:03:07,445 --> 02:03:12,615
These meats are from our animals.

761
02:03:15,361 --> 02:03:16,711
Bulghur...

762
02:03:17,314 --> 02:03:19,344
came from Konya.

763
02:03:21,432 --> 02:03:25,602
The plums in this sherbet
came from İzmir.

764
02:03:28,271 --> 02:03:34,911
Kayı Tent and Söğüt are the centers
of all ways.

765
02:03:36,418 --> 02:03:41,218
It's at the center of all trade ways...

766
02:03:41,818 --> 02:03:43,688
from İznik to Anatolia in Constantine.

767
02:03:50,147 --> 02:03:51,097
Now...

768
02:03:53,000 --> 02:03:58,120
what percentage of a tax
is given to Nikola...

769
02:03:59,473 --> 02:04:03,143
by a merchant
who wants to sell goods in İnegöl?

770
02:04:06,564 --> 02:04:08,334
Two fifths.

771
02:04:09,670 --> 02:04:12,050
Two fifths?

772
02:04:12,378 --> 02:04:17,368
And he promised to protect
you from me in return for it?

773
02:04:29,300 --> 02:04:31,810
Here I am.

774
02:04:32,504 --> 02:04:34,714
In front of you.

775
02:04:37,237 --> 02:04:41,357
You're in my tent.
You're sitting here.

776
02:04:42,459 --> 02:04:44,259
Tell me.

777
02:04:46,196 --> 02:04:49,306
Is it necessary to protect you from me?

778
02:04:56,109 --> 02:04:58,319
Is it?

779
02:05:07,579 --> 02:05:10,969
Do you know why you are here?

780
02:05:11,472 --> 02:05:13,152
If...

781
02:05:13,845 --> 02:05:16,565
you give up on your
collaboration with Nikola...

782
02:05:17,491 --> 02:05:22,171
I will forgive your life.

783
02:05:24,908 --> 02:05:30,058
And we will make a new trade agreement
for our friendship.

784
02:05:35,084 --> 02:05:38,264
My hostility brings death...

785
02:05:39,845 --> 02:05:43,845
and my friendship brings benefit.

786
02:05:47,912 --> 02:05:51,912
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come in.

787
02:05:56,648 --> 02:05:59,568
You should have a look, my Bey.

788
02:06:53,476 --> 02:06:55,656
Togay.

789
02:06:56,405 --> 02:06:57,815
Osman.

790
02:07:08,421 --> 02:07:10,361
Look...

791
02:07:10,713 --> 02:07:12,713
I'm alone.

792
02:07:14,555 --> 02:07:16,995
Are you here to die?

793
02:07:21,147 --> 02:07:24,957
Death only comes when I summon it.

794
02:07:30,727 --> 02:07:32,437
Alps.

795
02:07:33,459 --> 02:07:37,709
Be careful. Send some Alps around
the tent.

796
02:07:38,259 --> 02:07:41,879
It might be a trap.
Come on.

797
02:07:52,181 --> 02:07:55,231
I have his daughter.

798
02:07:56,624 --> 02:08:00,914
If you want her to
live, give the Lord to me.

799
02:08:14,943 --> 02:08:18,943
If you harm her...

800
02:08:20,400 --> 02:08:26,410
I will cut your bones off...

801
02:08:27,239 --> 02:08:30,309
and hang your skin on the entrance of the
tent.

802
02:08:32,143 --> 02:08:35,323
If you want Umur's daughter...

803
02:08:38,488 --> 02:08:43,428
bring your prisoner to Karaçayır...

804
02:08:44,544 --> 02:08:48,544
as long as I'm here, Osman Bey.

805
02:09:08,184 --> 02:09:10,604
As long as Togay lives...

806
02:09:14,307 --> 02:09:15,907
his daughter lives too.

807
02:09:16,328 --> 02:09:18,548
We once worshipped the same sky...

808
02:09:18,599 --> 02:09:22,079
with your generation, Osman Bey.

809
02:09:25,124 --> 02:09:28,064
The sky we worshipped is split.

810
02:09:28,323 --> 02:09:30,703
Now, our ways are
separated from each other.

811
02:09:31,305 --> 02:09:35,895
Only blood can clear those ways.

812
02:09:38,488 --> 02:09:44,718
When the time comes, we will continue
what our fathers have left unfinished.

813
02:09:57,326 --> 02:09:59,386
You kidnap women...

814
02:10:00,337 --> 02:10:02,787
like your father.

815
02:10:05,534 --> 02:10:09,164
I won't continue doing anything with
an ignoble like you.

816
02:10:13,949 --> 02:10:16,329
I...

817
02:10:17,225 --> 02:10:21,225
will cut you off under this blue sky.

818
02:10:32,621 --> 02:10:35,431
A good enemy is here.

819
02:10:36,389 --> 02:10:38,669
Bring the lord.

820
02:10:42,124 --> 02:10:47,174
If you make me wait here for long...

821
02:10:48,068 --> 02:10:52,528
you will hang her head as an ornament on
your tent.

822
02:11:02,609 --> 02:11:04,199
Can I...

823
02:11:06,050 --> 02:11:08,210
go now?

824
02:11:29,665 --> 02:11:31,605
Alps!

825
02:11:40,071 --> 02:11:51,341
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com